---
import ProductLayout from "../components/ProductLayout.astro";

const faq = [
  {
    question: "Does this replace Stripe Smart Retries?",
    answer:
      "No, we layer on top. Smart Retries picks the time-of-day inside Stripe's network. We pick the day-of-cycle and own the customer-facing emails.",
  },
  {
    question: "What happens on day 8?",
    answer:
      "We send the past-due notice and flip the subscription's metadata to alvey_dunning_status=past_due. We don't cancel, that's your call.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I customize the email copy?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Sender name, reply-to, logo, primary color, and full subject + body template per stage.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is my Stripe data sent anywhere?",
    answer:
      "OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest with Fernet. Recovery state lives in our database. No data leaves the system except the customer-facing email body.",
  },
  {
    question: "What if your service goes down on day 7?",
    answer:
      "Idempotent replay. When we come back up, day-7 fires once, not zero, not twice.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I customize the schedule?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Default is day 1 / 3 / 7 / 8, but you can configure any sequence per merchant.",
  },
];
---

<ProductLayout
  metaTitle="Stripe Failed Payment Recovery: branded, idempotent dunning"
  metaDescription="Automated dunning for Stripe Billing: branded retries on a schedule you control. Idempotent, audit-ready, $39/month flat per merchant."
  eyebrow="Marketplace App · Stripe"
  headline="Stop losing subscriptions to expired cards."
  subhead="Branded, idempotent dunning for Stripe Billing on the schedule you control. Day 1 retry, day 3 firmer, day 7 final, day 8 past-due notice: all under your brand."
  pricing="$39 / month flat · no per-recovery fee"
  ctaLabel="Install on Stripe"
  ctaHref="<Stripe Marketplace URL TBD>"
  secondaryCtaLabel="Watch 60-second demo"
  secondaryCtaHref="<Loom URL TBD>"
  problemTitle="Most failed payments aren't churn"
  whatYouGetTitle="What you get"
  whoForTitle="Who this is for"
  finalCtaTitle="Recover the revenue you've already earned."
  finalCtaSubhead="One-click Stripe Connect install. First recovery the same day."
  faq={faq}
>
  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      Most failed payments aren't churn, they're an expired card or a
      temporary hold from the issuer. The customer wanted to pay you. The
      card just didn't go through.
    </p>
    <p>
      The fix is a four-step retry sequence with branded, polite, well-timed
      emails. It's also the kind of thing that's annoying to build and even
      more annoying to keep running correctly under deploys, retries, and
      Stripe webhook replays.
    </p>
    <p>This app does it for you, idempotent by construction.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="what-you-get">
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Stripe Connect OAuth</strong>, one-click install, no API
        keys to handle.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Default 4-step dunning sequence</strong>, day 1 retry +
        gentle email, day 3 retry + firmer, day 7 final attempt, day 8
        past_due notice. Per-merchant schedule overrides.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Per-merchant email branding</strong>, logo, primary color,
        sender name, reply-to address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Custom email template overrides</strong>, full subject and
        body per stage if you want it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Idempotency-keyed retry ledger</strong>, append-only,
        replay-safe. Replayed cron tick? No-op. Mid-cycle redeploy? Safe.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Audit log per recovery</strong>, every retry attempt logged
        with timestamp, status, and the idempotency key that ran it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Per-merchant kill switch</strong>, pause dunning for any
        merchant in one click.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Subscription state tracking</strong>, active to past_due
        transitions are mirrored locally, not just hoped about.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Webhook signature verification</strong> and token encryption
        at rest with Fernet.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="who-for">
    <p>This app is for you if:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You run a SaaS or subscription business on Stripe Billing and lose
        more subscriptions to failed payments than you'd like.
      </li>
      <li>
        You want dunning emails customers see as coming from <em>your</em>
        brand, not a third-party tool.
      </li>
      <li>
        You care about idempotency and audit trails because your support team
        gets blamed when a customer gets two emails on the same day.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>It's not for you if:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You're not on Stripe Billing.</li>
      <li>
        You want a full revenue-recovery suite with phone calls, win-backs,
        and chat. We're focused on the email + retry layer specifically.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ProductLayout>
